{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"8814c6aabdae98c6","name":"card_unit_shark_mk_iii","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/CovertOp/units/card_unit_shark_mk_iii","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"SHARK Mk III","text":"Deployment: Deal damage to target enemy equal to other friendly air units.","flavorText":"The Blackburn Shark was a biplane torpedo bomber used by the British Royal Navy Fleet Air Arm during WWII. The aircraft was introduced in the mid-1930s and served primarily as a carrier-based reconnaissance and torpedo bomber aircraft. Despite its obsolescent design compared to contemporary monoplane aircraft, the Blackburn Shark played a significant role in maritime operations during the early years of the war. It saw action in various theaters, including the North Sea, the Mediterranean and the Atlantic Ocean, where it was used in reconnaissance missions, anti-submarine patrols and torpedo attacks against enemy shipping. While the Blackburn Shark was gradually phased out of frontline service as more advanced aircraft became available, it remained in use for training purposes and coastal defense duties throughout the war. A total of 269 Blackburn Shark’s were manufactured, including a few variants.","faction":"Britain","type":"bomber","rarity":"Rare","cost":2,"operationCost":1,"attack":1,"defense":2},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_shark_mk_iii","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_shark_mk_iii_title","SourceString":"SHARK Mk III","LocalizedString":"SHARK Mk III"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::bomber","attack":1,"defense":2,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_shark_mk_iii_text","SourceString":"Deployment: Deal damage to target enemy equal to other friendly air units.","LocalizedString":"Deployment: Deal damage to target enemy equal to other friendly air units."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_shark_mk_iii_history","SourceString":"The Blackburn Shark was a biplane torpedo bomber used by the British Royal Navy Fleet Air Arm during WWII. The aircraft was introduced in the mid-1930s and served primarily as a carrier-based reconnaissance and torpedo bomber aircraft. Despite its obsolescent design compared to contemporary monoplane aircraft, the Blackburn Shark played a significant role in maritime operations during the early years of the war. It saw action in various theaters, including the North Sea, the Mediterranean and the Atlantic Ocean, where it was used in reconnaissance missions, anti-submarine patrols and torpedo attacks against enemy shipping. While the Blackburn Shark was gradually phased out of frontline service as more advanced aircraft became available, it remained in use for training purposes and coastal defense duties throughout the war. A total of 269 Blackburn Shark’s were manufactured, including a few variants.","LocalizedString":"The Blackburn Shark was a biplane torpedo bomber used by the British Royal Navy Fleet Air Arm during WWII. The aircraft was introduced in the mid-1930s and served primarily as a carrier-based reconnaissance and torpedo bomber aircraft. Despite its obsolescent design compared to contemporary monoplane aircraft, the Blackburn Shark played a significant role in maritime operations during the early years of the war. It saw action in various theaters, including the North Sea, the Mediterranean and the Atlantic Ocean, where it was used in reconnaissance missions, anti-submarine patrols and torpedo attacks against enemy shipping. While the Blackburn Shark was gradually phased out of frontline service as more advanced aircraft became available, it remained in use for training purposes and coastal defense duties throughout the war. A total of 269 Blackburn Shark’s were manufactured, including a few variants."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::CurrentExpansion","hasD